description: Keep the generated Markdown command tree synchronized with every CLI change.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Command tree documentation

- Whenever commands are added, changed, or removed, update `docs/users/command-tree.md`
  in the same change. This includes configuration paths, operational and control
  commands, pipe modifiers, choices, hints, and argument syntax.
- Generate the document from the schemas with `python -m build_tools.command_tree`.
  Do not edit the generated tree by hand or maintain a separate command inventory.
- Run `python -m build_tools.command_tree --check` before committing command changes.
- Preserve Linux `tree` connectors and explicitly wrapped inline choices. Wrap
  between complete choices, align continuation lines, and do not rely on editor wrapping.
- When shared parser syntax changes outside the schemas, update the generator's
  parser-entry descriptions and tests so the document remains accurate.
